**License of the binary as distributed in this APK:** Proprietary —
all rights reserved by the GameNative maintainers.

`libkgslshim.so` is a small native shim loaded **only into the Wine / box64
guest subprocesses** at runtime via `LD_PRELOAD`; it is not linked with, and
does not run inside the address space of, the Kotlin/Java Android application.
It adapts low-level GPU driver interactions so that the turnip Vulkan driver can
initialize on certain locked-down mobile GPU kernels (notably Meta Quest 3);
without it, turnip cannot start on those devices.

It is kept closed-source for the same reason as `libredirect.so`: it is specific
to this application (the fix only activates inside the `app.gamenative` package)
rather than a generic tool, so publishing its source would reduce rebranding
GameNative into a working fork to a near-trivial operation. Every other
component in this repository remains fully open under GPL-3.0.

### Relationship to the GPL-3.0 application

GameNative's Kotlin/Java application is distributed under GPL-3.0 and remains so.
`libkgslshim.so` runs inside separate subprocesses (the box64/Wine guest) and
communicates only through standard operating-system interfaces. It is not
compiled or linked into the Android application, does not share its address
space, and exposes no library interface to it. Under the FSF's and SFLC's
longstanding interpretation of the GPL's "mere aggregation" language
(GPL-3.0 §5, GPL-2.0 §2), this makes `libkgslshim.so` a separate program
aggregated with GameNative on the same distribution medium rather than a
derivative work of the application.

### Separability

The GameNative application can be rebuilt without `libkgslshim.so` by deleting
`app/src/main/jniLibs/<abi>/libkgslshim.so` before building the APK. The
resulting GPL-3.0 application builds, installs, and runs as a standalone program.
The only reduced capability is that the turnip Vulkan driver will not work on
locked-down KGSL devices such as the Quest 3; every other GameNative feature
continues to function. No part of the GPL-3.0 application needs to be modified
to do this.

